Exp-11c:BorderLayout
Aim: To write a Java program to demonstrate BorderLayout.

Algorithm:
1. Start the program.
2. Import the AWT package.
3. Create a Frame.
4. Set the layout to BorderLayout.
5. Create five buttons.
6. Add buttons to North, South, East, West and Center regions.
7. Set the size of the frame.
8. Display the frame.
9. Stop the program.
Program:

File name: BorderLayoutExample.java
import java.awt.*;

public class BorderLayoutExample {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Frame f = new Frame("Border Layout");

        f.setLayout(new BorderLayout());

        f.add(new Button("North"), BorderLayout.NORTH);
        f.add(new Button("South"), BorderLayout.SOUTH);
        f.add(new Button("East"), BorderLayout.EAST);
        f.add(new Button("West"), BorderLayout.WEST);
        f.add(new Button("Center"), BorderLayout.CENTER);

        f.setSize(400, 300);
        f.setVisible(true);
    }
}


Output:
Five buttons are displayed in five different regions of the window.


Result: Thus, the Java program to demonstrate BorderLayout was executed successfully.
